><span> <span>$169.95</span></span> <span>at Best Buy</span></div></div></a></div></div><div><div></div><div><span class="hawk-tabletop-block-product-header">Best for sport</span><span>4. Sony LinkBuds Fit</span><span><div><span>☆</span><span>☆</span><span>☆</span><span>☆</span><span>☆</span></div></span><span>Robust, powerful sound</span><a href="#">Read more<span>▼</span></a></div><div><a aria-label="View Sony LinkBuds Fit on Newegg" href="#" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" role="link"><div><div><span> <span>$179.99</span></span> <span>at Newegg</span></div></div></a><a aria-label="View Sony LinkBuds Fit on Best Buy" href="#" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" role="link"><div><div><span> <span>$197.29</span></span> <span>at Best Buy</span></div></div></a><a aria-label="View Sony LinkBuds Fit on Walmart" href="#" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" role="link"><div><div><span> <span>$198</span></span> <span>at Walmart</span></div></div></a></div></div><div class="hawk-tabletop-footer-footer hawk-tabletop-footer-empty"></div></div></aside><p>Active noise cancellation (ANC) was once the preserve of high-end (or at least mid-range) headphones, but now it can be found even in budget pairs. And it can work very well indeed, for the money.</p><div></div><p>That qualifier is important. Because while you can't expect world-silencing exploits deployed by the likes of the <a href="#">Bose QuietComfort Ultra Headphones (2nd Gen)</a>, you can still effectively block out annoying outside noise, so you can hear your music more clearly, focus on work, or just have a snooze.</p><a></a><aside></aside><p>When we say "cheap", we mean under £150. It's all relative, see.</p><p>Our list includes all sorts of styles, including earbuds, over-ears and sports models.</p><div></div><p>During our reviews, we listen to a range of music and other content in a variety of settings to really gauge how each pair performs. We also test them against rival models at a similar price to see where they sit in the market, and each verdict is decided in consultation with other members of our reviews team to avoid individual bias.</p><p>For more on what our reviews process entails, see our <a href="#">how we test</a> section further down this page.</p><div> <div> <div> <span>Recent updates</span> </div> <p><strong>October 2026:</strong> We've swapped in the Sony WH-CH730N and updated the references to reflect the current Award winners.</p> </div> </div><div> <div> <div> </div> <div> <div class="person__name-socials"> <span>Joe Svetlik</span> </div> <aside>Contributor</aside> </div> <div><p>My first pair of noise-cancelling cans were the mighty Bose QuietComfort 2 in the early 2000s. I used them for everything, from working, to walking around town listening to music and getting some shut-eye on the red-eye. Thankfully <a href="#">noise-cancelling headphones</a> are now much cheaper than the QC2, making the tech more accessible to all. Whatever you want, you'll find a great – and affordable – pair from our list below, with extra features besides ANC, like great sound quality, good quality Bluetooth codecs and genuinely useful Bluetooth features like Multipoint.</p></div> </div> </div><a></a><h2>The best cheap noise-cancelling headphones we recommend in 2026</h2><p> <span>Why you can trust What Hi-Fi? </span> <span>Our expert team reviews products in dedicated test rooms, to help you make the best choice for your budget. <a href="#">Find out more about how we test.</a></span> </p><a></a><h3 class="article-body__section"><span>Best over-ears</span></h3><div> <div> <span> Image 1 of 11 </span> </div> <div> <div> <a href="#" aria-label="Image 1 of 11"> </a> <a href="#" aria-label="Image 11 of 11"> </a> </div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <figure> <div> <div> </div> </div> <figcaption> <span> (Image credit: What Hi-Fi?) </span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <button type="button"> </button> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <d